# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dirory — repository ignore rules
#
# Two rules of thumb here:
#   1. Never commit a real credential. `.env.example` is the only env file
#      that belongs in git; everything else is per-machine.
#   2. Commit things a user or teammate receives. The built plugin (`.rbz`)
#      is a deliverable, so `dist/` is NOT ignored — see the note further down.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# node
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# env — never commit real values
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
!.env.example

# supabase local state
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.log

# local type-check scaffolding
.tmpcheck/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
#
# `next build` output is regenerated on every deploy, so it is ignored.
# The plugin archive is NOT ignored: it is a shipped artefact (brief §105) and
# users install it directly, so it must live in the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/web/out/
apps/web/.next/
plugin/**/*.tmp

# Explicitly keep the built extension.
!dist/
!dist/*.rbz
